          %h2#local_2d_prequantum_boundary_field_theory_and_kkquantization Local 2d prequantum boundary field theory and KK-Quantization
          %h3#1_local_2d_prequantum_field_theory
            %strong 1)
            Local 2d prequantum field theory
          %p
            ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
          %p
            We use in there mostly just the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} full sub-(∞,1)-category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi DiffStack
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi SmoothGrpd
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Smooth
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  DiffStack \hookrightarrow SmoothGrpd \hookrightarrow Smooth \infty Grpd
          %p
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stacks"} differentiable stacks
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
            but as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            at least we also need
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth 2-groupoids
          %p
            In particular, write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+2-groupoid"} smooth 2-groupoid
            which is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+3-group"} circle 3-group
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields} \in \mathbf{H}
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi Fields
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi exp
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi i
                                %mi S
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 2
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{Fields}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{exp(i S)}}
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
                  }
          %p
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+action+functional"} local action functional
          %p
            (More generally we consider
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+super+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth super ∞-groupoids
            and replace
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
            by the moduli stack of
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+2-line+bundles"} super 2-line bundles
          %p
            Since this is necessarily a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizable+objects"} dualizable objects
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C2%29-category"} (∞,2)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category+of+correspondences"} correspondences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Corr
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Corr_2(\mathbf{H}, \mathbf{B}^2 U(1))
            it induces by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+theorem"} cobordism theorem
            a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum field theory
            given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-functor"} monoidal (∞,2)-functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Corr
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                          %mo ,
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 2
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Corr
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                          %mo ,
                          %mi KU
                          %mi Mod
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi exp
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi i
                                %mi S
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Bord
                            %mi n
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Fields
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Corr
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; Corr_2(\mathbf{H},\mathbf{B}^2 U(1)) &amp;\to&amp; Corr_2(\mathbf{H}, KU Mod)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\exp(i S)}}\nearrow&amp;  \downarrow
                  \\\
                  Bord_n &amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{Fields}}{\to}&amp; Corr_2(\mathbf{H})
                  }
          %p
            Here we postcomposed with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi gl
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi KU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi KU
                  %mi Mod
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
                  \\to
                  {\vert \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)\vert}
                  \\simeq
                  K(\mathbb{Z},3)
                  \\to
                  B gl_1(KU)
                  \\to
                  KU Mod
                  \\,.
          %h3#2_local_boundary_2d_prequantum_field_theory
            %strong 2)
            Local boundary 2d prequantum field theory
          %p
            Considering one marked boundary condition we have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
            defined in addition to the data of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo →
                  %mi KU
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(i S) \colon \mathbf{Fields} \to KU Mod
            by a morphisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Corr
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo ,
                  %mi KU
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Corr_2(\mathbf{H}, KU Mod)
            which as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            is of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Q
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi i
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi ξ
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi Fields
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi 𝕀
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi exp
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi i
                                %mi S
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; Q
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{i}}
                  \\\
                  \\ast &amp;&amp; \swArrow_{\mathrlap{\xi}} &amp;&amp; \mathbf{Fields}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\mathbb{I}}}\searrow
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\swarrow_{\mathrlap{\exp(i S)}}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+condition"} boundary condition
          %h3#QuantizationInKKTheory
            %strong 3)
            Quantization in KK-Theory
          %p
            We
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantize
            by interpreting the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/push-forward+in+generalized+cohomology"} push-forward in generalized cohomology
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+topological+K-theory"} complex topological K-theory
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi KU
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KU
          %p Specifically we quantize a correspondence as above by applying the following procedure
          %ol
            %li
              %p Decompose the correspondence explicitly as
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi Q
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↙
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo ↘
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi i
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo ⇙
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi ξ
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msup
                                      %mi i
                                      %mo *
                                    %mi χ
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Fields
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mi 𝕀
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo ↙
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi χ
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi KU
                              %mi Mod
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \&amp;&amp; Q
                      \\\
                      \&amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{i}}
                      \\\
                      \\ast &amp;\swArrow_{\mathrlap{\xi}}&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{i^\ast \chi}}  &amp;&amp; \mathbf{Fields}
                      \\\
                      \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\mathbb{I}}}\searrow
                      \&amp;&amp;
                      \\swarrow_{\mathrlap{\chi}}
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; KU Mod
                      }
                      \\,.
            %li
              %p
                Form
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+groupoid+convolution+algebras"} twisted groupoid convolution algebras
                to produce a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-span"} co-span
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+bimodules"} Hilbert bimodules
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi ξ
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi i
                            %mo *
                          %mi χ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi i
                            %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi χ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbb{C} \stackrel{\xi}{\to}
                      C_{i^\ast \chi}(Q)
                      \\stackrel{i^\ast}{\leftarrow}
                      C_\chi(X)
                      \\,.
              %p
                Regard this as a cospan in
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            %li
              %p
                Assume that the middle and right objects are
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizable+objects"} dualizable objects
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Th
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %mi χ
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi Q
                          %mo )
                        %mo )
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msub
                            %mi C
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi i
                                %mo *
                              %mi χ
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mi Q
                            %mo )
                          %mo )
                        %mo ∨
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Th(Q)
                      \\colon
                      \\left(C_{i^\ast \chi}\left(Q\right)\right)
                      \\to
                      \\left(C_{i^\ast \chi}\left(Q\right)\right)^{\vee}
              %p
                to the dual
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebra"} C*-algebra
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
                then this is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+isomorphism"} Thom isomorphism
                in this context.)
            %li
              %p
                Consider the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+morphism"} dual morphism
                to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi i
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^\ast
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo !
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msub
                            %mi C
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi i
                                %mo *
                          %mrow
